-/// validated and it is parsed again without validation.
+/// - The gltf crate only allows a required `EXT_texture_webp` behind its own feature, which reads
+///   the extension into a typed field that overrides `source`; this loader reads the extension's
+///   image itself (`prefer_extension_sources`). Validation reports every error, so when that is
+///   the only one the rest of the document validated and it is parsed again without validation.
+/// - An accessor with neither a bufferView nor sparse data is zero-filled (the spec allows it;
+///   blender exports morph targets like this), unless a `KHR_draco_mesh_compression` primitive
+///   reads it (its indices or an attribute): then the data is in a draco stream this loader
+///   cannot decode, and the load fails with an error naming the extension. The host repairs
+///   such a file by decoding those primitives and reloads it; a file that only lists the
+///   extension has nothing to decode, so its accessors stay zero-filled.
